# Single-page app fallback.
#
# The client routes /case/<slug> itself, but on a static host those paths are not
# files, so the host answers with its own 404 before the app ever loads. This
# serves index.html for any path that isn't a real file, with a 200 so it is not
# treated as an error page, and lets the router take over.
#
# Anything above this rule is matched first, which is where a redirect for a
# retired URL would go.

/*    /index.html    200
